{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#507","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#507","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#507\",\"parent_revision\":\"b3ea5fc43f7ab5e6254f5b369d2aca8a0ab76c15\",\"root_revision\":\"f655896a48c140b6eb5820750eb2fbf33aa93730cae89b520788ce02f02be4c8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe orchestrator-discipline plugin's PreToolUse hooks currently exclude .md files from the source file read warning, allowing the orchestrator to freely read and edit SKILL.md and references/*.md files. This creates a gap where the orchestrator bypasses delegation to /skill-creator or content optimizer agents for skill content modifications.\\n\\nObserved failure (session 2026-03-07): Orchestrator directly edited 4 skill reference files (back-links, cross-links, section merges, file moves) instead of delegating to agents. The hooks did not fire because .md files are in the exclusion list.\\n\\nNeeded: A new PreToolUse hook on Edit/Write that fires when the target path matches */skills/*/SKILL.md or */skills/*/references/*.md. The hook should inject additionalContext reminding the orchestrator to delegate skill content changes to /plugin-creator:skill-creator or contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer agents. Reading these files for routing decisions should remain allowed \u2014 only Edit/Write should be gated.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaim: plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks.json has matchers Read|Grep, Bash, Agent|Task \u2014 no Edit|Write matcher\\nTool: Read plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks.json\\nResult: 4 PreToolUse entries with matchers: Read|Grep, Bash, Bash, Agent|Task. No Edit|Write matcher confirmed.\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: pre-tool-orchestrator-read-warning.cjs SOURCE_FILE_EXTENSIONS has no .md extension\\nTool: Read plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/pre-tool-orchestrator-read-warning.cjs lines 17-18\\nResult: Regex: /\\\\.(py|toml|yaml|yml|js|cjs|mjs|ts|jsx|tsx|json|cfg|ini|env|sh|bash|go|rs|rb|java|c|cpp|h|hpp)$/i \u2014 .md absent\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: Existing hooks use data.agent_id check for subagent exclusion\\nTool: grep agent_id in pre-tool-orchestrator-read-warning.cjs\\nResult: Line 79: if (data.agent_id) \u2014 pattern confirmed\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\n\\nClaim: Session 2026-03-07 failure: orchestrator directly edited 4 skill reference files with no hook intervention\\nTool: Not directly verifiable from current state (session log not present)\\nverdict: UNVERIFIED \u2014 not required for implementation; the code gap is independently confirmed by hooks.json inspection\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: Extend orchestrator-discipline plugin to gate Edit/Write on skill content files\\nDate: 2026-04-19\\nGoal: Determine whether sufficient information exists to implement a new PreToolUse hook gating Edit/Write on skill content files.\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent (gate Edit|Write when path matches */skills/*/SKILL.md or */skills/*/references/*.md) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description\\n2. Gap confirmed (no Edit|Write matcher in hooks.json) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks.json: matchers are Read|Grep, Bash, Bash, Agent|Task \u2014 no Edit|Write present\\n3. .md files excluded from current read-warning (gap confirmed) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read pre-tool-orchestrator-read-warning.cjs lines 17-18: SOURCE_FILE_EXTENSIONS regex has no .md extension\\n4. subagent exclusion pattern | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: grep line 79: if (data.agent_id) \u2014 pattern verified in existing hook\\n5. Hook structure (additionalContext injection, exit 0, non-blocking) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: All 4 existing hooks use identical .cjs structure; agentskill-kaizen and other plugins provide precedents\\n6. Acceptance criteria | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Prior grooming 2026-04-15 defined 8 verifiable ACs\\nChanges from snapshot: No changes \u2014 all conditions were AVAILABLE in prior grooming. Only format update (Date + Decision fields).\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **extend orchestrator-discipline plugin to gate edit/write on skill content files** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-03-07 \u2014 orchestrator bypassed delegation for skill content edits\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 Score: 7/10\\nRationale: Skill content modification without delegation undermines the skill quality guarantee. The session 2026-03-07 failure (4 skill files edited without agent involvement) demonstrates the gap is exploitable. The fix is low-effort and high-value.\\nEffort: Small \u2014 one new .cjs hook file (~50-70 lines following existing hook pattern) and one line in hooks.json. Estimated: 2\u20133 hours.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `Edit(file_path=\\\"plugins/foo/skills/bar/SKILL.md\\\", ...)` in orchestrator session \u2192 `additionalContext` reminder to delegate to `/plugin-creator:skill-creator` or `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer`\\n2. `Write(file_path=\\\"plugins/foo/skills/bar/references/some-ref.md\\\", ...)` in orchestrator session \u2192 same reminder\\n3. `Edit(file_path=\\\"README.md\\\", ...)` \u2192 no reminder\\n4. `Read(file_path=\\\"plugins/foo/skills/bar/SKILL.md\\\", ...)` \u2192 no reminder (reads excluded)\\n5. Subagent session (hook input has `agent_id`) \u2192 no reminder for skill content paths\\n6. Hook exits 0 (non-blocking) in all cases\\n7. `plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks.json` updated with `Edit|Write` PreToolUse entry\\n8. `node ./hooks/pre-tool-skill-content-gate.cjs` with sample stdin \u2192 clean JSON output, no stderr\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nThe orchestrator-discipline plugin exists to enforce delegation discipline \u2014 the orchestrator should delegate implementation and content work to specialist agents. Gating Edit/Write on skill content files directly advances this mission: skill content modification requires specialist agents (/plugin-creator:skill-creator or contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer) that apply quality standards, citation requirements, and format validation the orchestrator cannot provide alone.\\n\\nThe gap being fixed (Edit/Write on .md skill files is ungated) is a scope omission from the original guardrail design, not a design conflict. The fix extends the existing pattern without altering its architecture.\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\nCitations: plugins/orchestrator-discipline/CLAUDE.md (\\\"No exemption categories: the orchestrator delegates, agents implement. This applies regardless of file type, change size, or perceived simplicity\\\"); hooks.json structure (additionalContext injection, non-blocking, agent_id exclusion \u2014 new hook follows identical pattern)\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: missing-guardrail\\nRationale: The orchestrator-discipline plugin is a guardrail system. The .md exclusion in the read-warning hook was correct for read operations (orchestrators may read markdown files for routing decisions), but it inadvertently left a gap: Edit/Write on skill content files (.md files under */skills/*/) also go unguarded. The guardrail for Edit/Write on skill content was never defined \u2014 this item adds it.\\nAnalysis method: intake-classification (design gap \u2014 exclusion that was correct for reads was incorrectly inherited by write operations)\\nScenario target: orchestrator-discipline plugin PreToolUse hooks\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED\\\\n\\\\n- Functional intent: PRESENT \\\\u2014 gate Edit/Write when path matches `*/skills/*/SKILL.md` or `*/skills/*/references/*.md`\\\\n- Scope: PRESENT \\\\u2014 non-blocking additionalContext injection, subagent sessions excluded via `data.agent_id`\\\\n- External interfaces: PRESENT \\\\u2014 `PreToolUse` hook, `Edit|Write` matcher, `file_path` confirmed in hooks-io-api skill\\\\n- Existing system: PRESENT \\\\u2014 all 4 hooks in `plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks.json` use identical .cjs structure with `data.agent_id` exclusion\\\\n- Gap confirmed by inspection: `plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks.json` matchers are `Read|Grep`, `Bash`, `Agent|Task` \\\\u2014 no `Edit|Write` matcher present\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Open an orchestrator session with the orchestrator-discipline plugin installed.\\n2. Call `Edit(file_path=\\\"plugins/foo/skills/bar/SKILL.md\\\", old_string=\\\"x\\\", new_string=\\\"y\\\")`.\\n3. Current behavior: no hook fires; edit proceeds without reminder.\\n4. Expected after fix: hook fires; additionalContext reminder injected before edit proceeds.\\n5. Observable evidence: presence of skill-content delegation reminder in hook output vs absence today.\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| File | Change | Scope |\\n|------|--------|-------|\\n| `plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks.json` | Add `Edit|Write` PreToolUse matcher entry | Modify |\\n| `plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/pre-tool-skill-content-gate.cjs` | New hook: path-match gate with additionalContext injection | Create |\\n| `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` | Version bump (auto-applied by pre-commit hook) | Auto-bumped |\\n\\n**Blast radius**: Minimal \u2014 one new .cjs file, one new hooks.json entry. No changes to existing hook files. Non-blocking hook (exit 0 always) with no workflow disruption. Subagent sessions excluded via data.agent_id check.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1e9d983bf43d262f00e8e4183fbea84132ac4508986180dce15ce5c10e04536a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg0a7g\"}"}